Mondays call in wistful waltz, with starry souvenirs;  
I draw my cloak from fur, with toast and stories.  
This morning swells with plans that call on my hands;  
I find my way, with a grin and a dash.

Tit for tat tidings, with routine in plain;  
Two hours on a task I'd flourished on.  
A nod from a friend, a wisp of my joy;  
I lay my sandbag down, with a "I did it."

Mondays call in sour waltz, with cold-souled knocks;  
I sit by my cup, and wait for my boss.  
Two hours on a task I'd flourished on;  
My body bows low, and my mind is on work.

